---
/**
 * The problem, as a paragraph rather than a row of stat tiles. The figures
 * and sources are the verified ones from the brief (data/content.ts SOURCES).
 */
---

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="problem-label">
  <div class="wrap grid">
    <h2 class="h2 lede" id="problem-label">During surgery, doctors often need to check the patient’s scans. They can’t touch the computer without breaking sterility, so they have to ask someone else to do it for them.</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>Operating-room time costs <span class="fig">$36–37 a minute</span><a class="ref" href="#ref-1">1</a>.</p>
      <p>
        Moving surgical guidance from a screen to sound cut screen time from <span class="fig">96% to 10%</span><a class="ref" href="#ref-2">2</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        After major liver surgery, <span class="fig">13%</span> of patients develop severe liver failure<a
          class="ref"
          href="#ref-3">3</a
        >.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /* A full sentence, so a step below the section display size. */
  .lede {
    grid-column: 1 / span 10;
    margin-bottom: var(--s-8);
    font-size: var(--fs-44);
    line-height: 1.12;
    max-width: 30ch;
  }
  .prose {
    grid-column: 5 / span 7;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s-3);
    font-size: var(--fs-28);
    line-height: 1.4;
    letter-spacing: var(--track-tight);
    color: var(--text-dim);
    max-width: 34ch;
  }
  .fig {
    color: var(--text);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .ref {
    font-size: 0.55em;
    vertical-align: super;
    margin-left: 0.15em;
    color: var(--text-dim);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .ref:hover {
    color: var(--text);
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .lede,
    .prose {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
    }
    .prose {
      font-size: var(--fs-20);
    }
  }
</style>
